WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:12.675
Messier 52 or M52, also known as NGC 7654 or the Scorpion Cluster, is an open cluster of stars in the highly northern constellation of Cassiopeia.

00:13.239 --> 00:16.979
It was discovered by Charles Messier in 1774.

00:17.374 --> 00:20.846
It can be seen from Earth under a good night sky with binoculars.

00:21.367 --> 00:26.637
The brightness of the cluster is influenced by extinction, which is stronger in the southern half.

00:27.259 --> 00:38.064
Its metallicity is somewhat below that of the Sun, and is estimated to be [Fe/H] = −0.05 ± 0.01.
